# 10. Create a Kubernetes Deployment

Create a file:

```text
deployment.yaml
```

Add:

```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment

metadata:
  name: kubernetes-web-deployment

spec:
  replicas: 2

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: kubernetes-web

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: kubernetes-web

    spec:
      containers:
        - name: web-container
          image: kubernetes-web-app:latest

          ports:
            - containerPort: 80

      imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
```

---

# 11. Understand the Deployment File

### API version

```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
```

Specifies the Kubernetes API version.

### Kind

```yaml
kind: Deployment
```

Tells Kubernetes that this file defines a Deployment.

### Name

```yaml
name: kubernetes-web-deployment
```

The Deployment is named:

```text
kubernetes-web-deployment
```

### Replicas

```yaml
replicas: 2
```

This tells Kubernetes:

> Keep **2 Pods** running.

### Container image

```yaml
image: kubernetes-web-app:latest
```

This is the Docker image that the Pods will run.

### Container port

```yaml
containerPort: 80
```

The Nginx container listens on port 80.

