# 24. Test Self-Healing

This is one of the biggest advantages of a Deployment.

First check the Pods:

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

Select one Pod and delete it:

```bash
kubectl delete pod POD_NAME
```

For example:

```bash
kubectl delete pod kubernetes-web-deployment-xxxxx-xxxxx
```

Now immediately run:

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

You will notice Kubernetes creates a replacement Pod.

Eventually:

```text
READY
2/2
```

again.

### Why?

Because the Deployment says:

```yaml
replicas: 2
```

Kubernetes continuously tries to maintain the desired state.

